<BODY STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">

<P STYLE="text-align: right; margin: 0"><B>Filed pursuant to Rule 424(b)(5)</B></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; text-align: right"><B>Registration No. 333-279942</B></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; text-align: right"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><B>Prospectus Supplement</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><B></B> (To Prospectus dated June 18, 2024)</P>


<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B><I>15,000,000 Class&nbsp;A Ordinary Shares</I></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B><I>&nbsp;</I></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B><I>And</I></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B><I>&nbsp;</I></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B><I>Up to 12,000 Class A Ordinary Shares by the
Selling Shareholder</I></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>Golden Heaven Group Holdings Ltd.</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">This is an offering of the securities of Golden
Heaven Group Holdings Ltd., a Cayman Islands holding company. As used in this prospectus supplement, terms such as the &ldquo;Company,&rdquo;
&ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us,&rdquo; &ldquo;our company,&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo; refer to Golden Heaven Group Holdings Ltd., unless
the context suggests otherwise, and when describing Golden Heaven Group Holdings Ltd.&rsquo;s consolidated financial information, such
terms shall also include the Chinese operating entities.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">We are offering 15,000,000 Class A ordinary shares
of par value US$0.125 each in the capital of the Company (the &ldquo;Class A Ordinary Shares&rdquo;), at a purchase price of US$1.80 per
share, pursuant to this prospectus supplement, the accompanying prospectus, and a share purchase agreement with the investors.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">This prospectus also relates to the resale by
certain selling shareholder described herein (the &ldquo;Selling Shareholder&rdquo;) of up to 12,000 Class A Ordinary Shares. The Selling
Shareholder may, from time to time, sell, transfer, or otherwise dispose of any or all of their Class A Ordinary Shares registered herein
on any stock exchange, market, or trading facility on which the Class A Ordinary Shares are traded or in private transactions. These dispositions
may be at fixed prices, at prevailing market prices at the time of sale, at prices related to the prevailing market price, at varying
prices determined at the time of sale, or at negotiated prices. We will not receive any of the proceeds from the sale or other disposition
of the Class A Ordinary Shares by the Selling Shareholder, but we will bear all costs, fees and expenses in connection with the registration
of the Class A Ordinary Shares offered by the Selling Shareholder. The Selling Shareholder will bear all commissions and discounts, if
any, attributable to the sale of the Class A Ordinary Shares offered for resale through this prospectus. For information regarding the
Selling Shareholder and the times and manner in which they may offer or sell Class A Ordinary Shares, see &ldquo;<I>Selling Shareholder</I>&rdquo;
and &ldquo;<I>Plan of Distribution</I>.&rdquo;</P>
<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">As of the date of this prospectus supplement,
the authorized share capital of the Company is US$200,600,000 divided into 1,600,000,000 Class A Ordinary Shares, and 4,800,000 Class
B ordinary shares with a par value of US$0.125 each (the &ldquo;Class B Ordinary Shares&rdquo;). Holders of Class A Ordinary Shares and
Class B Ordinary Shares have the same rights except for voting and conversion rights as set forth in our amended and restated memorandum
and articles of association currently in effect. In respect of matters requiring a vote of all shareholders, each holder of Class A Ordinary
Shares will be entitled to one vote per one Class A Ordinary Share and each holder of Class B Ordinary Shares will be entitled to two
hundred (200) votes per one Class B Ordinary Share. The Class B Ordinary Shares are convertible into Class A Ordinary Shares at any time
after issuance at the option of the holder on a one-to-one basis. As of the date of this prospectus supplement, we have 2,907,372 Class
A Ordinary Shares and 73,600 Class B Ordinary Shares issued and outstanding, respectively.</P>
<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Our Class A Ordinary Shares are listed on The
Nasdaq Capital Market under the symbol &ldquo;GDHG.&rdquo; On May 27, 2025, the last reported sale price of our Class A Ordinary Shares
on The Nasdaq Capital Market was US$1.81 per share.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The aggregate market value of our outstanding
Class A Ordinary Shares held by non-affiliates, or public float, as of March 28, 2025 (the &ldquo;Public Float Calculation Date&rdquo;),
was approximately US$353,037,100. This public float was calculated based on 2,972,944 Class A Ordinary Shares issued and outstanding on
the Public Float Calculation Date, all of which were held by non-affiliates, and a per share price of US$118.75. This price was the closing
price of our Class A Ordinary Shares on The Nasdaq Capital Market on March 28, 2025. Because the aggregate market value of our outstanding
Class A Ordinary Shares held by non-affiliates on the Public Float Calculation Date exceeded US$75 million, this registration statement
is considered filed pursuant to General Instruction I.B.1 of Form F-3, and the sales limitation set forth in General Instruction I.B.5(a)
of Form F-3 does not apply to offerings made hereunder.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></P>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 1; Options: NewSection -->
    <DIV STYLE="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <DIV STYLE="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">We are both an &ldquo;emerging growth company&rdquo;
and a &ldquo;foreign private issuer&rdquo; as defined under applicable U.S. securities laws and are eligible for reduced public company
reporting requirements. See &ldquo;<I>Item 3. Key Information&mdash;D. Risk Factors&mdash;Risks Related to Our Class A Ordinary Shares
and the Trading Market&mdash;For as long as we are an emerging growth company, we will not be required to comply with certain reporting
requirements, including those relating to accounting standards and disclosure about our executive compensation, that apply to other public
companies</I>&rdquo; and &ldquo;<I>Item 3. Key Information&mdash;D. Risk Factors&mdash;Risks Related to Our Class A Ordinary Shares and
the Trading Market&mdash;We are a foreign private issuer within the meaning of the rules under the Exchange Act, and as such we are exempt
from certain provisions applicable to U.S. domestic public companies</I>&rdquo; in the 2024 Annual Report.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">This is a self-underwritten offering. See &ldquo;<I>Plan
of Distribution</I>&rdquo; beginning on page S-9 of this prospectus supplement for more information regarding these arrangements.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>Investing in our securities involves risks.
See &ldquo;<I>Risk Factors</I>&rdquo; beginning on page S-3 of this prospectus supplement, page 10 of the accompanying prospectus and
&ldquo;<I>Item 3. Key Information&mdash;D. Risk Factors</I>&rdquo; in the 2024 Annual Report.</B></P>
<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>Neither the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission
nor any state securities commission nor any other regulatory body has approved or disapproved of these securities or determined if this
prospectus supplement is truthful or complete. Any representation to the contrary is a criminal offense.</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

